  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Routing policy",
      "items": [
        "route() returns glide → drex → jev: hosted only — local and modernbert are never auto-routed",
        "long input (past long_input_chars): glide and julia move to the back of the chain",
        "providers.route.enabled=false falls back to the legacy chain decide → jev",
        "by_task overrides, availability flags, and task allow-lists filter the chain per call"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Core roster — 8 providers",
      "items": [
        "decide · jev · drex · glide · julia · liquid · local · modernbert",
        "jev-class models (drex, glide, julia, liquid) inherit the jev head set via heads_for()",
        "glide, drex, jev speak /v1/systemone; decide is OpenAI-compatible; local + modernbert run in-process",
        "julia keeps top1-p confidence; liquid keeps the (N·max−1)/(N−1) statistic; both floor at 0.7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Candidates — 7, opt-in",
      "items": [
        "clm · openjev · kev · tev1 · laya · decide_1b · decide_multi",
        "disabled until named in providers.enabled; each speaks a wire that already exists",
        "flip the flag and point {pid}_api_url at the model — no code change"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Telemetry + calibration",
      "items": [
        "every call appends one JSONL record; a broken log never breaks the caller",
        "records carry answers, verdict, latency, tokens, http_status, retries, cost_usd, image_count",
        "record_feedback joins graded outcomes by input_sha256",
        "floors are refit only when a head qualifies — thresholds never transfer between providers"
      ]
    }
  ]
